From cda7b07502ec8e473df8efc86f04f6ca18ab9cb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leonieziechmann <48921293+leonieziechmann@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:04:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/15] =?UTF-8?q?fix(data):=20verifier=20round=202=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20""=20is=20absent=20for=20every=20optional=20key,=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?PDF/A-safe=20texts,=20total=20check(),=20nested=20marker=20with?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20data,=20faster=20decoder?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- decoder: an optional "" is absent whatever the key's type (a required one
  is empty); invoice-nr, subject and party names at most 4000 characters
  (PDF title/author in UTF-16), strings in custom bags at most 10 000,
  noncharacters U+nFFFE/U+nFFFF are issues; a cash discount has at most
  2 decimals
- schema: explicit Unicode White_Space class instead of \s/\S, "" counts as
  absent in the cross-field rules, maxLength for the metadata texts
- check() reports data that is no object instead of stopping; its bodies
  live in the lazy contract/api.typ
- payment(..): paid by transfer without an account is a data issue;
  payment-terms(discount:) on a credit note the data made is left out with
  an issue when hydrated
- a marker inside a marker's sample panics with data too
- result: rates rounded to 6 decimals, BT-1/BT-44 as the XML states them
- frame.typ prints sender.management given as lines (crashed before)
- signature test: comment/string-aware scanner, any identifier, rejects an
  argument sink; wired into tests.yaml
- decoder hot path: fewer calls (region scan, inline dates and item-id,
  precomputed limits, cheaper amount guard); reports byte-identical

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RaaQussN1QVEE8zRWeeCD3
